    {
      "v": 2,
      "zh": "就去见所罗巴伯和以色列的族长，对他们说：「请容我们与你们一同建造；因为我们寻求你们的　神，与你们一样。自从亚述王以撒哈顿带我们上这地以来，我们常祭祀　神。」",
      "en": "they came to Zerubbabel and the leaders[NOTE:1] and said to them, “Let us help you build,[NOTE:2] for like you we seek your God and we have been sacrificing to him[NOTE:3] from the time[NOTE:4] of King Esarhaddon[NOTE:5] of Assyria, who brought us here.”[NOTE:6]",
      "notes": [
        "Heb “the heads of the fathers.” So also in v. 3.",
        "Heb “Let us build with you.”",
        "The translation reads with the Qere, a Qumran MS, the LXX, the Syriac Peshitta, and the Arabic version וְלוֹ (velo, “and him”) rather than the Kethib of the MT, וְלֹא (veloʾ, “and not”).",
        "Heb “days.”",
        "Esarhaddon was king of Assyria ca. 681-669 b.c.",
        "The Assyrian policy had been to resettle Samaria with peoples from other areas (cf. 2 Kgs 17:24-34). These immigrants acknowledged Yahweh as well as other deities in some cases. The Jews who returned from the Exile regarded them with suspicion and were not hospitable to their offer of help in rebuilding the temple."
